lity, concentration, problem solving, but also arrogance, hot temper, weak leadership, loner, moody. So D still has concerns.\n\nWe need to decide whether to maintain vote for C or shift. Likely maintain C, but we need to address D's decision-making evidence. We can argue that while D shows good problem solving, the lack of reliability evidence and the negative traits (arrogance, hot temper) still make C stronger. Also we can note that A's technical competence is good but lacking reliability and stress resilience. So C remains best.\n\nThus public message: I agree with C, note D's decision-making evidence but still lacking reliability, and his interpersonal concerns. Also note A's technical competence but missing reliability and stress resilience. So maintain vote for C.\n\nWe must output METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
